diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c95f988..d2ea3a1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -18,4 +18,14 @@ Build and interface details: [documentation](https://unixnu.com/drivers/gop-fram
 
 Display traces obtain physical addresses from prepared direct-display slots. Validation records use address zero until a slot is mapped; the flip record supplies the mapped address. Observers do not prepare memory or query unwired descriptors.
 
+## Isolated nezha iPhone27 integration
+
+This branch retains the current upstream fence refusal/target/cancellation and frame-trace behavior, and keeps the previously qualified first 32 CPU frame scans. `NativeGOPWire.h` is byte-identical to the CPU baseline. No SM8550 DPU operation is enabled by this integration.
+
+An optional `native_adreno_gpu_rendering_active()` board provider preserves CPU presentation before a Metal renderer is discoverable. Its false-to-true transition is monotonic until reboot: after publication an unknown, busy or timed-out GPU fence stays pending. The A840 board sets the release/acquire flag before registering the accelerator. The host fence tests exercise both this gate and the upstream refusal cases; hardware behavior is not yet qualified.
+
+The iPhone27 adapter reads plane0 width, height, row bytes, size and data offset through the original IOSurface routines, including the nonplanar fallback. It bounds that view within the descriptor and requires the base and offset to agree; extended-pixel origins remain refused. CPU copies and diagnostics use the view's data start. GPU offers carry the offset and size internally, map only the page-aligned view, and cache by descriptor, task, offset and length. Non-page-aligned views use the CPU path. The wire format and its mapping ID remain unchanged, so the existing Metal client can be retained. DPU scanout is still disabled for this port.
+
+`python3 Test/check-plane-view.py --output <new-workspace-directory>` runs the actual offer/wait/cache/completion methods with mocked IOKit mappings, and checks bounded CPU copies from a nonzero offset. It does not establish real system GPU presentation.
+
 The macOS display attributes, the timing and color elements and the hot plug state follow the display driver of [macOS-DroidVM](https://github.com/Droid-VM/macOS-DroidVM), the DroidVM port booted with UniXNU.
